160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E ( What made Ingenuity special was not only its historical achievements, but also the sensors it has to support its companion, the Perseverance rover. Ingenuity surprised everyone by operating far beyond its planned 30-day mission. It continued working for three years, contributing to many discoveries and setting seven new records. After overcoming countless challenges throughout its long mission, Ingenuity finally suffered damage to its blades on the harsh surface of Mars. However, its journey was not over yet, as it still had something valuable to offer humanity.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (Thanks to the software uploaded before its final flight, Ingenuity is expected to continue collecting valuable data for the next 20 years, as long as no unexpected problems occur. Every day when the sun rises, it will record the movements of the surrounding sand and take temperature measurements. Future astronauts and robotic vehicles visiting Mars will be able to access this data and use the information collected by Ingenuity in NASA's future projects, such as SkyFall, Mars Chopper and Dragonfly.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
